<section class="section cobble-calculator" id="cobble-calc" aria-labelledby="cobble-tool-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 id="cobble-tool-title">Estimate cobbles by the face you will lay</h2>
      <div class="section-divider"></div>
      <p>Switch between a paved surface and one straight border run. The finished face, joint, and cutting allowance determine the count; freight and pallet estimates use your supplier's numbers.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="calc-wrapper">
      <div class="calc-panel">
        <div class="calc-panel-title"><h3>1. Choose the layout</h3></div>
        <div class="cobble-options" aria-label="Project layout">
          <button type="button" class="choice active" data-cobble-mode="paving" aria-pressed="true">Driveway apron, path, or patio</button>
          <button type="button" class="choice" data-cobble-mode="edging" aria-pressed="false">One edging or curb run</button>
        </div>

        <div class="dim-grid" id="cobble-paving-fields">
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-length">Paved length</label>
            <input type="number" id="cobble-length" value="10" min="0.1" max="10000" step="any" inputmode="decimal" />
            <span class="unit-label">feet</span>
          </div>
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-width">Paved width</label>
            <input type="number" id="cobble-width" value="10" min="0.1" max="10000" step="any" inputmode="decimal" />
            <span class="unit-label">feet</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dim-grid" id="cobble-edging-fields" hidden>
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-run">Length of one border run</label>
            <input type="number" id="cobble-run" value="50" min="0.1" max="10000" step="any" inputmode="decimal" />
            <span class="unit-label">linear feet</span>
          </div>
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-direction">Face along the run</label>
            <select id="cobble-direction">
              <option value="length">Block length (9 in in this example)</option>
              <option value="width">Block width (5 in in this example)</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="field-note">For two driveway sides or separate runs, calculate each run and add the counts. Each run has its own end cuts.</p>

        <div class="calc-panel-title"><h3>2. Match the supplier's stone</h3></div>
        <div class="cobble-options stone-options" aria-label="Stone size examples">
          <button type="button" class="choice active" data-cobble-stone="regular" aria-pressed="true"><strong>Large cobble</strong><small>9 × 5 in paving face</small></button>
          <button type="button" class="choice" data-cobble-stone="cube" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Cobble cube</strong><small>4 × 4 in paving face</small></button>
          <button type="button" class="choice" data-cobble-stone="jumbo" aria-pressed="false"><strong>Belgian block</strong><small>10 × 7 in paving face</small></button>
        </div>
        <div class="dim-grid">
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-face-length">Visible face length</label>
            <input type="number" id="cobble-face-length" value="9" min="0.1" max="60" step="any" inputmode="decimal" />
            <span class="unit-label">inches</span>
          </div>
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-face-width">Visible face width</label>
            <input type="number" id="cobble-face-width" value="5" min="0.1" max="60" step="any" inputmode="decimal" />
            <span class="unit-label">inches</span>
          </div>
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-joint">Planned joint</label>
            <input type="number" id="cobble-joint" value="0.5" min="0" max="3" step="any" inputmode="decimal" />
            <span class="unit-label">inches</span>
          </div>
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-extra">Extra for cuts and sorting</label>
            <input type="number" id="cobble-extra" value="8" min="0" max="50" step="any" inputmode="decimal" />
            <span class="unit-label">percent</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="field-note">The size buttons change only the face dimensions; the joint stays at the value you entered. Check the planned joint for each product, especially small cubes. These are nominal examples, and rough or reclaimed faces can vary.</p>

        <div class="calc-panel-title"><h3>3. Add supplier details if available</h3></div>
        <div class="dim-grid">
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-piece-weight">Weight per piece (optional)</label>
            <input type="number" id="cobble-piece-weight" placeholder="From product or quote" min="0.01" max="10000" step="any" inputmode="decimal" />
            <span class="unit-label">lb</span>
          </div>
          <div class="input-field">
            <label for="cobble-pallet-size">Pieces per pallet (optional)</label>
            <input type="number" id="cobble-pallet-size" placeholder="From supplier" min="1" max="100000" step="1" inputmode="numeric" />
            <span class="unit-label">pieces</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="field-note">Leave these blank if you buy by the piece. A quoted pallet capacity and piece weight can differ by color, quarry, and finish.</p>
      </div>

